EFFECT SIZES  (change in reported net Sharpe, clean -> corrupted)
=================================================================
The strategy's net Sharpe over each dataset's own reporting window. The sign is
secondary: + flatters, - degrades returns or shifts to a weaker window; the
MAGNITUDE is how far the reported number strays. Weigh it against the s.e. below
- small moves are noise. The detection matrix above is the robust result.
defect                      sev        clean  corrupt   delta   caught by
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
wrong_side_asof             high        0.64     2.11   +1.47   asof
llm_cutoff_overlap          critical    0.64     1.59   +0.95   cont
lookahead_signal            critical    0.64     1.17   +0.53   caus
cost_too_low                high        0.64     1.05   +0.41   plau
shared_scaler               high        0.64     0.69   +0.05   fold
warmup_live_window          medium      0.64     0.65   +0.01   warm
survivor_only_universe      high        0.64     0.62   -0.02   surv
latest_vintage_fundamentals high        0.64     0.62   -0.03   fund
unpurged_cv                 high        0.64     0.60   -0.04   purg
forward_adjusted_qfq        medium      0.64     0.58   -0.06   adj
unadjusted_split            high        0.64    -0.13   -0.77   adj
single_calm_quarter         medium      0.64    -1.54   -2.19   regm
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
clean baseline net Sharpe 0.64 over 520 days (Lo 2002 iid s.e. ~0.76); cost 20 bps
a |delta| below ~0.76 (one s.e.) is not distinguishable from noise at this sample size

Notes on the small / negative deltas (all are real defects, all caught above):
  - each sub-signal is 1/5 of the blended composite, so a leak in one (unpurged
    CV, shared scaler, restated fundamentals) barely moves the blended Sharpe
    even as the guard flags it at the source.
  - forward_adjusted_qfq moves price LEVELS only; returns (hence Sharpe) are
    unchanged by construction - a data-integrity defect, not a Sharpe lie.
  - unadjusted_split DEGRADES the Sharpe: the strategy trades the fake -50% split
    jumps and loses. A negative delta is still a corrupted backtest.
  - llm_cutoff_overlap / single_calm_quarter change the WINDOW, not the signal;
    the sign depends on which window, which is exactly why coverage must be
    audited structurally rather than trusted from one number.

