GAPS  (defects no guard flagged in this run)
============================================
'no guard' = nothing in the suite targets this input domain, so it is the next
script to write. 'gate did not bind' = a guard ran but its pass/fail threshold
was not crossed here - a limitation of the gate, not a missing script.
  none: every defect is caught by at least one guard.

